WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.009
So let's talk about corona virus deaths for
weeks, almost for two months.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:11.340
The right and the anti science crowd were
telling us, don't worry, cases are up, but

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.090
deaths aren't going to go up.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.710
And we would say, why not?

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.950
And they would come up with explanations like,
well, listen, you know, it's young people

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.500
now who are getting the virus.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.860
Young people don't get very sick.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.920
They don't go into the hospital.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.450
They don't die.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.430
So even though cases are spiking starting
in mid-June, we're not going to see a spike

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.020
in deaths.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.730
Some others would say it's a less serious
strain.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.590
Now, the virus is mutated and it's far less
serious now.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.750
Others said we're better at treating it.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.750
Deaths won't go up.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:46.760
We've got, you know, Hydroxy and Rham Desi
vier and we're just not going to see that

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.020
death spike because we're better at treating
it.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:56.920
Well, for the like the tenth time in the last
month, we again have set a 30 to 60 day new

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.510
high water mark in terms of deaths.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:07.280
And yesterday, fourteen hundred eighty five
people died of Corona virus, 14, 85.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.190
That's half a 9/11 in a single day.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:14.580
This is the most deaths yesterday since May
27.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.820
There are about 64 days.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:23.470
We are quickly losing all the progress that
was made during April and early May.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.460
We're back at the May 27 death number.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.700
If you look at the brown line on the graph
that we have up on the screen, that's the

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.240
seven day moving average.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.159
So sometimes looking at individual days can
be less than a complete picture because we

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:41.240
tend to get less reporting on the weekends.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:46.420
So if you look at a seven day average, you
can see that the seven day moving average

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:51.020
of deaths has been climbing since right around
the Fourth of July holiday here in the United

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.100
States.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.799
That should have been a signal that things.

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:57.410
Weren't being done correctly, it has now been
almost a month since then.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:01.650
As you probably know by now, deaths are a
lagging indicator to cases.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.380
So even if we believe that cases started to
flatten on July 16th.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:11.879
Now, many of us don't believe that because
that's the day on which reporting from hospitals

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:16.629
shifted from going to the CDC, instead going
to Trump's Department of Health and Human

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:17.629
Services.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:23.540
But if you believe that case has started to
flatten on July 16th, then that means we are

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:29.579
still weeks from the peak in terms of single
day deaths.

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:35.909
And that means that 10 or 14 days from now,
the daily death toll could be once again tragic.

00:02:35.909 --> 00:02:40.939
It could get to a 9/11 every day or just short
of it.

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:48.280
Now, as you know, as it's almost become apocryphal
at this point, but I've been saying Massachusetts

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.040
has handled the virus quite well.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.010
But if you're all in the same pool and someone's
peeing in the deep end and you're in the shallow

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.169
end, eventually you're going to get some of
that pee in the shallow end.

00:02:59.169 --> 00:03:01.579
If you understand what I'm saying, eventually
it's going to reach you.

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:02.590
We're all in the same pool.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:07.090
And even here in Massachusetts, it's a slow
uptick, but there is an uptick.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.889
And it started in mid-July.

00:03:08.889 --> 00:03:13.559
We had, you know, 175, 200 cases a day for
weeks.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:18.230
We're now more regularly getting 300, 325
cases a day.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:23.950
And we're about to see, is it 50000, is it
100000, 150000 college students flying in

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.180
over the next four weeks to start college
and add to that that we're about to get hit

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.200
with the flu season in the United States.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.669
I'm seeing CBS and Walgreens advertising flu
shots.

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:36.940
I'm going to get mine very soon.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:43.219
This could be ramping up to arguably the worst
or most difficult fall in the United States

00:03:43.219 --> 00:03:45.290
from a public health standpoint.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:50.999
I will just say in a very long time, does
it go all the way back to 1918 and the flu?

00:03:50.999 --> 00:03:51.999
I'm not sure.

00:03:51.999 --> 00:03:55.959
But certainly in decades, people just aren't
listening.

00:03:55.959 --> 00:03:58.090
Much of the world did handle this.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.389
This was not the only way that it could have
gone the trajectory in the United States.

00:04:02.389 --> 00:04:07.340
I hate that it has become political, but because
Donald Trump did fail us.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:09.459
He has to suffer the consequences.

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:12.200
He has to be removed in November.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.349
I don't even need a president that will do
anything that special.

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:16.950
We just need one that will do.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:22.260
I was just interviewed actually on a New Zealand
program, and we'll be posting that very soon

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.900
to YouTube and Facebook.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.010
Jacinda Ardern in New Zealand.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.810
She didn't bring any unique medical knowledge.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:33.660
She just realized that she shouldn't pretend
to know things she doesn't know.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:39.970
She's going to defer to the doctors and let
the doctors lead the way with her support.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.370
That's all I need a president to do.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.480
But we are now back where we were months ago.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.610
We're sort of starting from scratch in a sense.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.620
There are discussions about needing a full
lockdown reset to get things under control.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.470
I don't think there's any political appetite
for that at this point in time.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:59.360
And think about all of the people who stayed
home for months, sacrificed financially, sacrificed,

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.320
you know, psychologically and emotionally
to flatten the curve.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.330
We're back to where we were back then.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.600
And we are still up against mass evictions,
growing unemployment.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.240
Consider the disrespect, by the way, to the
health care workers.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.470
Remember, they're heroes.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.470
We appreciate them.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.470
Right?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.240
Well, then why isn't everybody wearing a mask?

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.320
How is it respectful to health care workers
to walk around with no mask and to have indoor

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:27.120
dining and have casinos open in movie theaters?

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.380
We haven't done the right thing for them as
much as for the victims of the virus.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.410
It's disgusting.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.660
It's tragic.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.830
And the next three months, it could be really
bad.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.430
It could be really, really bad.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:42.590
And I want to hear what's going on in your
state.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.460
I am on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.490
Let me know how you see it.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:45.570
Let me know what's taking place.

